  "title": "Oklo's Groves Reactor Achieves First Criticality in Under a Year",
  "summary": "Oklo achieves first criticality less than a year after groundbreaking through the U.S. Department of Energy’s Reactor Pilot Program. The Groves low-power test reactor is the first reactor under the program to achieve criticality on private land, built from the ground up on a greenfield site. The Groves facility establishes the operational foundation for future commercial isotope production. The project proves American nuclear deployment timelines can be measured in months rather than years. Oklo",
